column2:
That was the first part of our journey. 

Now accompany me safely to {%t:0D}.

{%V:06} {%N:07}

column3:
Esta foi a primeira parte da nossa viagem.

Agora acompanha-me sao e salvo até {%t:0D}.

{%V:06} {%N:07}

column2:
Enough of these stressful deals.

In the hope that I have not overtaxed your patience please now take me to {%t:0D}.

{%V:06} {%N:07}

column3:
Chega destes negócios cansativos.

Na esperanca de nao ter abusado da tua paciência, leva-me agora a {%t:0D}.

{%V:06} {%N:07}

column2:
{%V:0E} {%N:0F},

The map was divided into nine pieces among the crew and we spread out in all directions of the compass. No idea where the other pieces are, but I'll keep my ears open.

{%V:0C} {%N:0D}

column3:
{%V:0E} {%N:0F},

O mapa foi dividido em nove pedacos entre a tripulacao, e espalhámo-nos aos quatro ventos. Nao faco ideia de onde estao os outros pedacos, mas vou manter os ouvidos atentos.

{%V:0C} {%N:0D}

column2:
You have fulfilled the mission and shall receive the reward as agreed!

Thank you very much!

{%V:0A} {%N:0C}

column3:
Cumpriste a missao e receberás a recompensa combinada!

Muito obrigado!

{%V:0A} {%N:0C}

column2:
Dear {%5:00}{%N:07},

News of the successes of our tranquil town has spread far beyond the town's borders. Now evil powers, full of malice, are planning to rob us of our best by demanding a contribution of the fruit of our hard labour. It has been reported to us that a large army of mercenaries is on its way, and that these fiends will overrun us, murdering, plundering, and burning.Let us take precautionary measures to protect our homes, since we can no longer turn back the bloody storm.

The Town {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Caro {%5:00}{%N:07},

A fama dos êxitos da nossa pacata cidade espalhou-se muito para lá das suas fronteiras. Agora forcas malignas, cheias de malícia, planeiam roubar-nos o melhor exigindo uma parte do fruto do nosso duro trabalho. Foi-nos comunicado que um grande exército de mercenários vem a caminho e que esses demónios cairao sobre nós matando, saqueando e incendiando. Tomemos precaucoes para proteger os nossos lares, pois já nao podemos desviar a tempestade sangrenta.

A cidade de {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Citizens of  {%t:04}!

Hordes of marauding foreign troops are sweeping through towns, robbing and murdering without mercy. There is no limit to their atrocities. Whether our prayers - that they might refrain from coming to our beautiful town - have been heard, is yet uncertain.
Arm yourselves, reinforce the walls, and stand bravely with your arms!May the walls hold as steadfastly as our courage!

The Town {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Cidadaos de {%t:04}!

Hordas de tropas estrangeiras saqueadoras varrem as cidades, roubando e matando sem piedade. As suas atrocidades nao têm limite. Ainda nao se sabe se as nossas preces - que poupem a nossa bela cidade - foram ouvidas.
Armai-vos, reforcai as muralhas e resisti com coragem de armas na mao! Que as muralhas se aguentem tao firmes como a nossa coragem!

A cidade de {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Dear Sir,

On their last shore leave, the crew was sitting in a tavern as usual when a drunken sailor bawled out stories about the ship's kobold through the room. He talked about his last ship that was taken by the ship's kobold, and that he was the only one to escape. You know, I do not pay a lot of attention to this superstition but the crew has been a little restless since then. I have got the situation under control and merely wanted to submit a report. 

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Senhor,

Na última licenca em terra, a tripulacao estava sentada como de costume numa taberna, quando um marinheiro bêbedo se pôs a berrar pela sala histórias sobre o duende do navio. Contou que o seu último navio foi levado pelo duende e que ele foi o único a escapar. Sabes que nao dou muito crédito a essa supersticao, mas desde entao a tripulacao anda um pouco inquieta. Tenho a situacao sob controlo e só queria dar-te parte.

O timoneiro do {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

These credulous scary-cats have again picked up something about the ship's kobold. This invisible spirit supposedly protects each and every ship, and that should it leave the ship, it would go down with crew and cargo. You know the legend that a ship's kobold shows himself before he leaves a ship. However, these credible sailors now see him grinning from behind every plank. The morale is not very good, that's why you should see about it yourself!

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Senhor,

Estes medrosos crédulos voltaram a ouvir falar do duende do navio. Esse espírito invisível protegeria todo o navio, e se alguma vez o abandonasse, este iria ao fundo com homens e carga. Conheces a lenda de que o duende se mostra antes de abandonar um navio. Mas agora estes marinheiros crédulos veem-no a sorrir por trás de cada tábua. O moral nao anda bom, por isso é melhor veres tu mesmo!

O timoneiro do {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

This cowardly pack has fled. Here in {%t:08} many sailors have discharged, except for a few courageous ones, due to fear of the ship's kobold. For better or for worse, you will have to engage a new crew before you can set sail again.

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Senhor,

Este bando de cobardes fugiu. Aqui em {%t:08} muitos marinheiros desembarcaram com medo do duende, tirando uns poucos valentes. Queiras ou nao, terás de contratar uma nova tripulacao antes de podermos zarpar de novo.

O timoneiro do {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

There is talk of unusual sightings near the town of {%t:08}. Several sailors, independent of each other, are said to have seen a ghost ship gliding across the sea and this, despite a calm wind. The crew's heart dropped to the sole of their feet, but they are bravely carrying out their duties. I have doubled the guard to keep things quiet.

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Senhor,

Fala-se de avistamentos estranhos perto de {%t:08}. Vários marinheiros, sem se conhecerem, dizem ter visto um navio fantasma a deslizar sobre o mar, e isto com vento calmo. A tripulacao caiu o coracao aos pés, mas cumprem com coragem o seu dever. Dobrei a guarda para manter a calma.

O timoneiro do {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

The fairy tale of the ship's kobold is again doing the rounds among the crew. I have heard of cases where the crew worked itself into such a state, that the whole ship was put in danger. I will be harder on the sailors than normal so that they get rid of this dangerous superstition from their heads as soon as possible.

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Senhor,

O conto do duende do navio corre de novo entre a tripulacao. Ouvi falar de casos em que os homens se exaltaram tanto que puseram todo o navio em perigo. Serei mais duro do que o costume com os marinheiros, para que tirem quanto antes da cabeca essa perigosa supersticao.

O timoneiro do {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

Some of the older sailors are telling the younger ones, that the ship's kobold leaves all ships whose shipping line does not deal in a god fearing way. I was able to put aside the on setting restlessness among the crew, by telling them that you are the most honest trader in the entire Hanse. Everyone is now concentrating on their work on board.

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Senhor,

Alguns marinheiros mais velhos contam aos mais novos que o duende abandona todos os navios cujo armador nao comercia com temor a Deus. Consegui acalmar a inquietacao nascente na tripulacao dizendo-lhes que és o comerciante mais honesto de toda a Hansa. Agora todos se dedicam ao seu trabalho a bordo.

O timoneiro do {%s:09}

column2:
{%7:00},

The passenger that we took on board in {%t:01} and were supposed to be taking to {%t:0A} has disappeared! I've had the crew scour the ship from the keel to the crow's nest, but there was no trace of him to be found anywhere.

Helmsman of the {%s:06}

column3:
{%7:00},

O passageiro que embarcámos em {%t:01} e devíamos levar a {%t:0A} desapareceu! Mandei a tripulacao revistar o navio da quilha ao cesto da gávea, mas nao havia rasto dele em parte alguma.

O timoneiro do {%s:06}

column2:
{%7:00}{%N:07},

Thank you for your help. Please obtain the following goods for me and get them to {%t:05}, in good condition and within 20 days:

{%B:09}{%w:10}
{%B:0A}{%w:11}
{%B:0B}{%w:12}
{%B:0C}{%w:13}
{%B:0D}{%w:14}
{%B:0E}{%w:15}

Store the goods there, in your trading office. I will have them collected at the given time.

{%V:16} {%N:06}

column3:
{%7:00}{%N:07},

Obrigado pela tua ajuda. Arranja-me por favor as seguintes mercadorias e leva-as a {%t:05}, em bom estado e no prazo de 20 dias:

{%B:09}{%w:10}
{%B:0A}{%w:11}
{%B:0B}{%w:12}
{%B:0C}{%w:13}
{%B:0D}{%w:14}
{%B:0E}{%w:15}

Armazena-as lá, no teu escritório. Mandarei buscá-las na altura combinada.

{%V:16} {%N:06}

column2:
Estate of Mr Jakob Blank

Last night, Mr Jakob Blank died of natural causes in his {%t:09} home. He does not leave any descendants, and his recently amended will and testament names the {%R:00} Leopold Jantzen as his sole heir. An examination of his estate reveals that Jakob Blank, who ended his days living in impoverished circumstances, had a promissory note in the amount of 500,000\C.
The full amount will be sent to you forthwith.

The Town Treasurer, {%t:09}
{%+:09}

column3:
Heranca do senhor Jakob Blank

Ontem à noite, o senhor Jakob Blank faleceu de morte natural na sua casa em {%t:09}. Nao deixa descendentes, e o seu testamento, recentemente alterado, nomeia o {%R:00} Leopold Jantzen herdeiro único. O exame da heranca revela que Jakob Blank, que terminou os seus dias na pobreza, possuía uma letra no valor de 500.000\C.
A soma integral ser-vos-á enviada sem demora.

O tesoureiro da cidade de {%t:09}
{%+:09}

column2:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Last time we came ashore in {%t:07}, the crew was sitting in the inn as usual when some drunken sailor started bellowing stories about the Kobold around the room. He talked about his last ship, which was taken by the Kobold, and how he was the only person that managed to escape. You know, I don't set much store by these myths, but your crew has been on tenterhooks ever since. I have the situation under control and simply wanted to let you know.

Helmsman of the {%s:04}

column3:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Da última vez que desembarcámos em {%t:07}, a tripulacao estava sentada na estalagem como de costume quando um marinheiro bêbedo se pôs a berrar pela sala histórias sobre o duende do navio. Contou que o seu último navio fora levado pelo duende e que ele foi o único que conseguiu escapar. Sabes que nao dou grande crédito a estes mitos, mas desde entao a tua tripulacao anda com os nervos em franja. Tenho a situacao sob controlo e só te queria avisar.

O timoneiro do {%s:04}

column2:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Strange sightings have been reported near {%t:07}. Several sailors have claimed on separate occasions that they have seen a ghost ship gliding through the waves under full sail, even though there was no wind. When they heard this, the crew's hearts sank, but they bravely continued with their duties. I have assigned twice as many guards as usual in an attempt to stop them worrying.

Helmsman of the {%s:04}

column3:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Foram relatados avistamentos estranhos perto de {%t:07}. Vários marinheiros afirmaram, em ocasioes diferentes, ter visto um navio fantasma a deslizar sobre as ondas de velas enfunadas, apesar de nao haver vento. Ao ouvir isto, a tripulacao perdeu o ânimo, mas continuou corajosamente com as suas tarefas. Dupliquei os turnos de vigia para tentar sossegá-la.

O timoneiro do {%s:04}

column2:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

The cowardly rabble has fled. While we have been here in {%t:08}, every sailor except me has jumped ship for fear of the Kobold. You will have to enlist a new crew before we can set sail again, whether you want to or not.

Helmsman of the {%s:04}

column3:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

A cobarde ralé fugiu. Enquanto estivemos aqui em {%t:08}, todos os marinheiros menos eu desertaram com medo do duende. Queiras ou nao, terás de contratar uma nova tripulacao antes de podermos voltar a zarpar.

O timoneiro do {%s:04}

column2:
Most esteemed {%R:01} {%n:01},

As we can see from Rostock, you certainly don't stint on your deeds. So we hope you will accept another sum by way of thanks, which you can invest in the town's further improvement right away. This time it is {%c:00}.

The Alderman {%F:00}{%+:03}

column3:
Estimadíssimo {%R:01} {%n:01},

Como vemos em Rostock, nao poupas esforcos. Por isso esperamos que aceites mais uma quantia em agradecimento, que podes investir de imediato no progresso da cidade. Desta vez sao {%c:00}.

O vereador {%F:00}{%+:03}

column2:
Worthy {%R:01} {%n:01},

You have not betrayed our confidence in you at all - on the contrary: Stettin is positively flourishing. So please take these {%c:00} for your future projects. This gold was donated by wealthy former traders to the Hanseatic League to be used for whatever purpose you wish.

The Alderman {%F:00}{%+:03}

column3:
Digno {%R:01} {%n:01},

Nao traíste de modo nenhum a nossa confianca, pelo contrário: Stettin está verdadeiramente florescente. Aceita entao estes {%c:00} para os teus projetos futuros. Este ouro foi doado à Hansa por ricos antigos comerciantes, para ser usado para o fim que desejares.

O vereador {%F:00}{%+:03}

column2:
Welcome, {%R:01} {%n:01},

Stockholm has once again become a magnificent town and we have you to thank for this. Take these {%c:00} as a token of our appreciation.

Your Alderman {%F:00}{%+:03}

column3:
Bem-vindo, {%R:01} {%n:01},

Stockholm voltou a ser uma cidade magnífica, e devemo-lo a ti. Aceita estes {%c:00} como sinal do nosso apreco.

O teu vereador {%F:00}{%+:03}

column2:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

So I've been waiting and waiting and still no sign of my daughter? I was certainly wrong about you. Fine, I'll try and find her myself. I still have some hope.

{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}

column3:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

Espero e espero e ainda nem sinal da minha filha? Enganei-me redondamente a teu respeito. Pois bem, vou tentar encontrá-la eu mesmo. Ainda tenho alguma esperanca.

{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}

column2:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

This is the end for me! The last pleasure in my life has been sunk with that pirate {%N:06}'s cog! How could you have let that happen? May this deed be an onerous burden on your conscience forever!

{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}

column3:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

E o meu fim! A última alegria da minha vida afundou-se com a coca daquele pirata {%N:06}! Como pudeste deixar que isso acontecesse? Que este ato pese para sempre na tua consciência!

{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}

column2:
To all long distance traders!

Arsonists have turned our town into a flaming inferno, and we are very short of raw materials for rebuilding it. In order to increase our supplies of iron goods and bricks, previously stored fur stocks are being offered at reasonable prices in the market square.

Mayor of {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
A todos os comerciantes de longa distância!

Incendiários transformaram a nossa cidade num inferno de chamas, e faltam-nos muito as matérias-primas para a reconstruir. Para aumentar as nossas reservas de ferragens e tijolos, as peles armazenadas sao oferecidas a precos razoáveis na praca do mercado.

O presidente da câmara de {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
{%R:01} {%n:01},

I need your help! The wells in my town have been contaminated and now there is a plague raging relentlessly through the streets. I know you've already done a lot for my friends and me, but I beg you just to keep an eye on things, so that my lovely town is still well provided for.

Mayor of {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
{%R:01} {%n:01},

Preciso da tua ajuda! Os pocos da minha cidade foram contaminados e agora a peste grassa sem piedade pelas ruas. Sei que já fizeste muito pelos meus amigos e por mim, mas peco-te que vás vigiando a situacao, para que a minha bela cidade continue bem abastecida.

O presidente da câmara de {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Dear {%R:01} {%n:01},
The upturn of the Hanseatic League is complete! How can we ever thank you enough? You have saved the Hanseatic League and given new powers to the community. The townspeople will never forget you!

The Alderman {%F:00}{%+:0D}

column3:
Caro {%R:01} {%n:01},
A prosperidade da Hansa está completa! Como te poderemos alguma vez agradecer o suficiente? Salvaste a Hansa e deste novas forcas à comunidade. Os cidadaos nunca te esquecerao!

O vereador {%F:00}{%+:0D}

column2:
Dear {%R:06} {%n:06},

Not very long ago, a terrible plague afflicted our town. Could you help us to rebuild London again? You will receive a handsome sum as payment if London can attract 1,000 new permanent residents and be restored to its former splendour.

The Mayor of London{%+:01}

column3:
Caro {%R:06} {%n:06},

Há nao muito tempo, uma terrível peste atingiu a nossa cidade. Poderias ajudar-nos a reconstruir London? Receberás uma bela quantia como pagamento se London atrair 1.000 novos residentes permanentes e recuperar o seu antigo esplendor.

O presidente da câmara de London{%+:01}

column2:
Dear {%R:06} {%n:06},

Thank you for helping us to rebuild London again. By way of thanks, I have had several deliveries of surplus wool brought to your trading office in Rostock.

The Mayor of London{%+:01}

column3:
Caro {%R:06} {%n:06},

Obrigado por nos ajudares a reconstruir London. Em agradecimento, mandei levar ao teu escritório em Rostock várias remessas de la excedente.

O presidente da câmara de London{%+:01}

column2:
Our saviour, {%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

What a wonderful blessing - you have liberated Stettin from the evil pirate. Now the long distance traders can put in at our town again without fear. Be assured of our eternal gratitude. We cannot give you gold, but we will reward you by filling your trading office with barrels of beer.

Mayor of Stettin{%+:03}

column3:
Nosso salvador, {%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

Que bêncao maravilhosa: libertaste Stettin do malvado pirata. Agora os comerciantes de longa distância podem voltar a aportar na nossa cidade sem medo. Conta com a nossa eterna gratidao. Ouro nao te podemos dar, mas recompensar-te-emos enchendo o teu escritório de barris de cerveja.

O presidente da câmara de Stettin{%+:03}

column2:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

The pirate outside Stettin has not been seen again and only the Kobold himself knows what could have happened. But that isn't our problem, and we are hoping with all our hearts that the pirate will stay missing.

Mayor of Stettin{%+:03}

column3:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

O pirata diante de Stettin nao voltou a ser visto, e só o próprio duende do navio sabe o que pode ter acontecido. Mas isso nao é problema nosso, e esperamos de todo o coracao que o pirata continue desaparecido.

O presidente da câmara de Stettin{%+:03}

column2:
Dear {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

It has come to our attention that some of the Dutch King's saboteurs have settled in {%t:01}. They probably want to prevent the Hanseatic League regaining its former position of power. Keep an eye on your stocks of goods! As soon as we know where these miscreants are lurking, we will contact you again.

The Hanseatic League council{%+:05}

column3:
Caro {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Chegou-nos ao conhecimento que alguns sabotadores do rei da Holanda se instalaram em {%t:01}. Querem provavelmente impedir a Hansa de recuperar a sua antiga posicao de poder. Vigia as tuas reservas de mercadorias! Assim que soubermos onde se escondem esses malfeitores, voltaremos a contactar-te.

O conselho da Hansa{%+:05}

column2:
To all traders from Rostock,

An underhand act of sabotage destroyed all of the town's grain stocks as well as those belonging to some traders today. A search for the culprits is currently underway.

The Mayor{%+:01}

column3:
A todos os comerciantes de Rostock,

Uma sabotagem traicoeira destruiu hoje todas as reservas de cereais da cidade, bem como as de alguns comerciantes. Os culpados estao a ser procurados.

O presidente da câmara{%+:01}

column2:
To all traders from Rostock,

The saboteurs have struck again.

The Mayor{%+:01}

column3:
A todos os comerciantes de Rostock,

Os sabotadores voltaram a atacar.

O presidente da câmara{%+:01}

column2:
Dear {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Our suspicions were right. It seems that the mayor of Bruges was coerced into the wicked acts by a councillor called {%N:0A} with forged documents. The councillor himself was commissioned by the Dutch King to worm his way into the mayor's confidence, with a view to weakening the Hanseatic League through piracy and sabotage. As far as we can tell, the mayor of Bruges is not to blame at all, however the corrupt {%N:0A} has escaped.

The Hanseatic League council{%+:05}

column3:
Caro {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

As nossas suspeitas estavam certas. Parece que o presidente da câmara de Bruges foi forcado àqueles atos vis por um conselheiro chamado {%N:0A}, por meio de documentos falsificados. O próprio conselheiro fora encarregado pelo rei da Holanda de ganhar a confianca do presidente da câmara, para enfraquecer a Hansa com pirataria e sabotagem. Tanto quanto podemos ver, o presidente da câmara de Bruges nao tem culpa nenhuma; o corrupto {%N:0A}, porém, fugiu.

O conselho da Hansa{%+:05}

column2:
Dear {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Thank goodness! It is over! {%N:0A}, the wicked Dutchman, has finally been destroyed! Now the oceans and towns are safer places again and nothing else can stand in the way of the Hanseatic League's growth.

The Hanseatic League council{%+:05}

column3:
Caro {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Gracas a Deus! Acabou! {%N:0A}, o malvado holandês, foi finalmente destruído! Agora os mares e as cidades voltam a ser mais seguros e já nada se opoe ao crescimento da Hansa.

O conselho da Hansa{%+:05}

column2:
{%7:03},

Last time we came ashore in {%t:07}, the crew was sitting in the inn as usual when some drunken sailor started bellowing stories about the Kobold around the room. He talked about his last ship, which was taken by the Kobold, and how he was the only person that managed to escape. You know, I don't set much store by these myths, but your crew has been on tenterhooks ever since. I have the situation under control and simply wanted to let you know.

