{%7:03},

Essa cobarde ralé fugiu. Enquanto estivemos aqui em {%t:08}, todos os marinheiros menos eu desertaram com medo do duende. Queiras ou nao, terás de contratar uma nova tripulacao antes de podermos voltar a zarpar.

O timoneiro do {%s:04}

column2:
Greetings,

The problems that we assigned you to deal with have been resolved. Our friends have urged us to settle the conflict in a peaceful, civilised manner.

{%N:09}

column3:
Saudacoes,

Os problemas que te encarregámos de resolver estao resolvidos. Os nossos amigos instaram-nos a resolver o conflito de forma pacífica e civilizada.

{%N:09}

column2:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

Your ship, {%s:05}, is riddled with barnacles. This means that the condition of your ship is much worse than previously thought.

Harbour-master of {%t:07}

column3:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

O teu navio, o {%s:05}, está cheio de cracas. Isto significa que o estado do teu navio é muito pior do que se pensava.

O capitao do porto de {%t:07}

column2:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

It has come to our attention that the planks on your ship, {%s:05}, are in a much worse condition than previously thought. You are therefore strongly advised to have your ship repaired.

Harbour-master of {%t:07}

column3:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

Chegou ao nosso conhecimento que as tábuas do teu navio, o {%s:05}, estao em muito pior estado do que se pensava. Aconselhamos-te, pois, vivamente a mandar reparar o navio.

O capitao do porto de {%t:07}

column2:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

It has been ascertained that the damage to your ship, {%s:05}, is much more serious than previously thought. It is in your own interests that we advise you to have the ship repaired as soon as possible.

Harbour-master of {%t:07}

column3:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

Apurou-se que os danos no teu navio, o {%s:05}, sao muito mais graves do que se pensava. No teu próprio interesse, aconselhamos-te a mandar reparar o navio o mais depressa possível.

O capitao do porto de {%t:07}

column2:
The pirate has been killed, but not by one of your ships!
So you are hardly entitled to the reward I promised you.

{%V:08} {%N:07}

column3:
O pirata foi morto, mas nao por um dos teus navios!
Por isso dificilmente tens direito à recompensa que te prometi.

{%V:08} {%N:07}

column2:
Hear ye! Oh Hear ye, citizens!

Tidings of our peaceful town's success have spread far beyond the city limits. Now despicable evil forces are plotting against our interests, demanding that we hand over the merchandise that we have worked so hard to produce. It is coming to our attention that a huge army of mercenaries will soon be coming to inundate us with murder, fire and looting.
We need to take precautions quickly to protect our homes, for we suspect there will be no way of averting this bloodthirsty assault.

The town of {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Ouvi! Ouvi, cidadaos!

A notícia do êxito da nossa pacífica cidade espalhou-se muito para lá das muralhas. Agora, vis forcas malignas conspiram contra os nossos interesses e exigem que entreguemos as mercadorias que tanto nos custou produzir. Chega-nos a notícia de que um enorme exército de mercenários virá em breve inundar-nos de assassínios, fogo e saque.
Temos de tomar precaucoes depressa para proteger as nossas casas, pois suspeitamos que nao haverá maneira de evitar este assalto sanguinário.

A cidade de {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Citizens of {%t:04}!

Hordes of marauding mercenaries are sweeping through the land, leaving murder and pillage in their wake. No atrocity is beyond them. Who knows whether our prayers will be answered, so that they may leave our beautiful town alone?
So prepare yourselves, fortify the walls and stand by your arms.
May the walls and our courage hold!

The town of {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Cidadaos de {%t:04}!

Hordas de mercenários saqueadores varrem o país, deixando atrás de si assassínios e pilhagem. Nenhuma atrocidade os detém. Quem sabe se as nossas preces serao ouvidas e deixarao em paz a nossa bela cidade?
Preparai-vos, pois, fortificai as muralhas e estai prontos com as armas.
Que as muralhas e a nossa coragem resistam!

A cidade de {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Our gruelling business in {%t:08} is now complete.
I trust this has not tried your patience too much, and I would be grateful if you would now take me to {%t:00}.

Courier on board the {%s:05}

column3:
Os nossos extenuantes assuntos em {%t:08} estao concluídos.
Espero que isto nao tenha posto demasiado à prova a tua paciência, e ficar-te-ia grato se agora me levasses a {%t:00}.

O mensageiro a bordo do {%s:05}

column2:
Dear Sir or Madam,

The Hanseatic League is delighted to announce that a race will be taking place on {%D:01} between the Hanseatic League's boldest traders!
The voyage begins in {%t:15} and takes the participants to {%t:18}. Curious onlookers are more than welcome to attend the race.
The following traders are taking part in the race:

